# Local build output (per machine — see .cargo/config.toml and ~/.zshenv).
/target
**/target

# Rust
*.pdb

# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: a "C:" directory.
# If a bare `cargo` ever runs on Linux WITHOUT CARGO_TARGET_DIR set, cargo reads
# the Windows target-dir "C:/rust-build/sector" as a *relative* path and creates
# ./C:/rust-build/sector/ right here ON THE NAS, then builds over SMB. We want
# that stray "C:" folder to show up LOUDLY in `git status`, not be hidden. So we
# do NOT add it to this file. If you see one, the ambient override didn't fire.
